# Maps USF people to GitHub usernames, so a student signing in with Google is
# registered in one step and never sees the GitHub question.
#
# A Google Forms export works unchanged -- keep the header row and drop the
# file in as-is:
#
#   Timestamp,Email Address,What is your GitHub username?
#   2026/08/20 9:14:02 AM,jsmith@dons.usfca.edu,jsmith
#
# Columns are found by header name when a header is present ("github" for one,
# "email"/"user"/"usf" for the other); otherwise the first column is the USF
# identity and the last is the GitHub username.
#
# The USF side may be a full address or just the username, and matching is
# case-insensitive and ignores the domain -- so "benson" here matches someone
# signing in as benson@usfca.edu or benson@dons.usfca.edu.
#
# Install as /etc/classnet/roster.csv (it is gitignored: it is student data).
usf_email,github
benson@usfca.edu,gdbenson
